WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.360
On November 27th, 2011, a comet was&nbsp;
spotted traveling towards Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.480
This comet's existence was confirmed by Mount&nbsp;
John University Observatory on December 1st&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:17.680
of that year, and the next day, the Minor&nbsp;
Planet Center gave it a name - Comet C/2011 W3.&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.000
Scientists continued to observe this comet's&nbsp;
trajectory, which appeared to be nothing out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
of the ordinary. That is, until C/2011 W3 reached&nbsp;
perihelion. C/2011 W3, like many objects entering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.680
the solar system, had been pulled into orbit&nbsp;
around the sun, and perihelion is a scientific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.520
term which refers to the point at which an object&nbsp;
in orbit is the closest to the star it's orbiting.&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.240
On December 13th, as C/2011&nbsp;
W3 approached perihelion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.440
Solar Dynamics Observatory observed a fragment&nbsp;
splitting off from the main body of the comet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.600
a fragment that then began hurtling&nbsp;
towards Earth. Despite the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.480
Foundation's implementation of deterrence&nbsp;
procedures, the comet stayed its course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:05.600
and soon it became clear that areas near the&nbsp;
predicted crash site would have to be evacuated.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.480
On December 21st, the comet reached the&nbsp;
Earth, crashing into the Pacific Ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:17.040
124 kilometers off the coast of the United States.&nbsp;
This in itself wasn't unusual - on average,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.600
our planet is hit by 17 pieces of space&nbsp;
debris a day, and much of it does land&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.960
in the ocean. What was unusual, however, was&nbsp;
that 3 days later, the creature that had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.240
riding that piece of space debris reached&nbsp;
land and revealed itself to the world.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.280
Starting on December 24th, 2011, footage&nbsp;
started cropping up all over the internet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:44.160
of an otherworldly creature. It appeared to be an&nbsp;
enormous deer, with mint-green fur, a long neck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:50.240
human face, and marbled black antlers ringed&nbsp;
by floating ice crystals and metallic spheres.&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.000
The SCP Foundation quickly mobilized&nbsp;
in order to contain the beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.440
but it was immediately evident&nbsp;
that it was impervious to attacks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.640
What was worse, it had a devastating&nbsp;
way of retaliating against aggressors.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.000
Fitting its cosmic origins, The Deer possesses&nbsp;
the godlike ability to instantly transmute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:14.400
matter through powerful energy beams. It can&nbsp;
turn solids into liquids, gases into solids, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:20.160
organic material into metal instantaneously. The&nbsp;
materials that result from these transmutations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.680
remain stable, despite outside factors that&nbsp;
logically should destabilize them. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.640
The Deer can create shapes made of solid&nbsp;
frozen hydrogen that remain solid even outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:36.160
of the sub-zero temperatures that it normally&nbsp;
requires to keep gases in their solid states.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.320
This transmutation ability is used&nbsp;
consciously, as a form of attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.840
and the beams occur in a variety&nbsp;
of shapes around the creature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.880
The most common are a vertical column measuring&nbsp;
five to seven meters in diameter and sixty to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.840
eighty meters in height, or a horizontal&nbsp;
cone, measuring between one hundred and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:59.200
one hundred and fifty meters in length and ten&nbsp;
to thirty meters in width at the furthest end.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.200
Although The Deer rarely attacks without&nbsp;
provocation, it will transmute matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.480
indiscriminately, making no effort to exclude&nbsp;
non-combatants from the range of the attack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.680
Everything within the range&nbsp;
of attack is transmuted.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.360
People hit with the beam will be transformed into&nbsp;
hexagonal columns roughly 2.4 meters in height,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:25.120
known as SCP-2845-1. These columns have rubbery&nbsp;
green skin, and no organs outside of a brain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:30.160
which makes up the entirety of the column's&nbsp;
inside. Miraculously, they remain alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:36.240
as the brains of instances of SCP-2845-1 have&nbsp;
been studied and are shown to be in a constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:42.160
state of high activity. Analysis of brainwave&nbsp;
patterns suggests a pattern of call and response,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:48.720
which implies a telepathic link between&nbsp;
the different instances of SCP-2845-1.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.720
Given the devastating effects&nbsp;
of SCP-2845's attacks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:58.000
the SCP foundation naturally had an extremely&nbsp;
difficult time containing it, and they had to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.600
take drastic measures to do so. The Foundation&nbsp;
enlisted the help of the Global Occult Coalition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:08.160
as well as outside consultants who were brought&nbsp;
in to try and draft a plan for containment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.960
the beast. The ideal place for its containment&nbsp;
was determined to be somewhere on the other side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:17.360
of the Sierra Nevada mountains, and through a&nbsp;
campaign of artillery bombardment that lasted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:24.640
from December 26th 2011 to January 15th&nbsp;
2012, the SCP and GOC were able to drive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:31.840
SCP-2845 across the mountains to the location&nbsp;
that would come to be known as Site 100.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:36.960
What sets site 100 apart from other SCP&nbsp;
containment sites is the complex system&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:43.840
put in place in order to properly keep SCP-2845 in&nbsp;
containment. The site consists of nine concentric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:49.680
circular bands, designated Ring-A through&nbsp;
Ring-I, with a gap located between Ring-C&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:58.320
and Ring-D. Six circular chambers are located&nbsp;
at 0, 60, 120, 180, 240, and 300 degrees within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.760
each Ring and Gap. The chambers located at&nbsp;
0 degrees are aligned with geographic north.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.840
Two additional circular chambers are located&nbsp;
outside of Ring-I, located at 120 and 240&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:15.520
degrees. The floor of each circular chamber is&nbsp;
decorated with a hexagram, or 6-pointed star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:24.640
made of lead. The central chamber, containing&nbsp;
SCP-2845 and 216 instances of SCP-2845-1, is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:34.320
contain an atmosphere of 96.3% hydrogen, 3.25%&nbsp;
helium, and .45% ammonia maintained at -110°C.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:41.360
Site 100 must be staffed at all times by a minimum&nbsp;
of 30 trained individuals, who are to be given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.440
unlimited access to untrained human subjects. The&nbsp;
staff and subjects must perform a complex series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:53.680
of rituals at different points of the circle,&nbsp;
acting on a cycle of 63 hours and 54 minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:59.120
Each ritual lasts 39 minutes, and they&nbsp;
must be performed every 10 hours. At the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:03.200
beginning of each new cycle, the schedule&nbsp;
of rituals will be carried out in the next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:08.720
ring closest to the containment chamber, going&nbsp;
from Ring-I inwards until they reach Ring-A.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.840
Each ritual requires 6 participants.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.160
Procedure 410-Constantin is performed&nbsp;
at the 60 degree point on the circle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:22.960
Containment specialists are presented with&nbsp;
masks - Joy, Sadness, Anger, Apathy, Fear, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:28.960
Foolishness – and must act out a farcical, comedic&nbsp;
play before playing a dice game with one another.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:34.320
Procedure 420-Perinaldo is performed at&nbsp;
the circle's 120 degree point. This ritual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:40.400
involves a performance by a band consisting of&nbsp;
flute, oboe, clarinet, French horn, timpani,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:45.120
and bass drum. It must be a live&nbsp;
performance, recordings have no effect.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.640
Procedure 430-Epimetheus, performed at the&nbsp;
180 degree point, involves exchanging small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:56.960
gifts with values not exceeding 4.28 USD. Each&nbsp;
gift exchange is followed by the recitation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:02.240
of ceremony Epimetheus-A and followed by&nbsp;
scattering grain over the chamber floor.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:06.000
Procedure 440-Cassiel, performed at 240 degrees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.880
involves the recitation of ceremony Cassiel-A&nbsp;
while participants bind their feet with wool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.440
and drink 500 milliliters of olive oil.&nbsp;
They then will break apart a rock weighing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:20.880
at least 200 kilograms with hammers.&nbsp;
Ceremony Cassiel-B is recited throughout.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.280
While the previous procedures might sound weird,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.840
it's after that point that the containment&nbsp;
rituals start to take a turn for the gruesome.

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:33.360
Procedure 450-Cairo is performed at&nbsp;
the 300 degree point. In this ritual,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:37.280
a D-class personnel has a symbol drawn&nbsp;
on their stomach with a platinum-based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.960
paint - a ring surrounding a dot, with an&nbsp;
arrow pointing upwards at the 90 degree point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.280
The D-class is then presented with&nbsp;
a blue cloak, crown, and scepter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:53.360
before being restrained in a chair and castrated&nbsp;
with a hand sickle as ceremony Cairo-A is recited.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:59.760
Finally, 460-Omphalos is performed at the&nbsp;
0 degree point, the very top of the circle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:06.480
This ritual, the most gruesome of all, involves&nbsp;
cooking and eating a three-month old infant.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:10.800
In case of containment breach, site&nbsp;
100 is equipped with a nuclear warhead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:16.560
just like all SCP containment sites, which&nbsp;
will be detonated if containment ever fails.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:21.600
Because of the complexity of the&nbsp;
procedures required to contain SCP-2845,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.640
some animosity started to develop between the&nbsp;
Foundation personnel stationed at site 100&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.920
and the outside contractors who had conceived the&nbsp;
containment rituals. They had to go through these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:38.080
time-consuming, elaborate, sometimes horrific&nbsp;
procedures over and over again, going around and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:43.680
around the circular maze that made up the site,&nbsp;
every 10 hours, and there was no way of being able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.320
to tell if the things they were doing had any&nbsp;
effect on the creature in containment at all.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.600
On the 31st of January, 2012, Site Director&nbsp;
Dell finally approached one of the containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.880
consultants and asked him why, exactly,&nbsp;
they had to uphold all this pageantry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.480
Surely there had to be some other, more&nbsp;
streamlined way of keeping the creature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.480
in containment. The consultant denied&nbsp;
this, and explained their reasoning -

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.400
“I find it sickening that after all&nbsp;
the struggle to contain this creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:15.440
pencil-pushing bureaucrats are still seeking&nbsp;
to cut corners where they cannot be afforded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:21.120
to be cut... The ritual will remain as it&nbsp;
is, and will not be changed in any way.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.320
Rituals do not work because of some underlying&nbsp;
laws, such as those that science operates on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:31.920
Rituals work because they are rituals. They&nbsp;
work because an arbitrary set of criteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:36.400
has been met with exacting care. Belief&nbsp;
that meeting these arbitrary criteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:40.640
achieves a certain end assigns power to&nbsp;
the ritual. The actions that were once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.520
meaningless now have been assigned Meaning&nbsp;
through their repetition and application.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:52.880
This is how one seals away a god, and this&nbsp;
is a god. I know that the Foundation does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:58.560
not approve of using the term, but it&nbsp;
is still the case. The Stag is a god,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:02.880
and it is not a petty local god. It&nbsp;
is not one of the mild gods of Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.720
or some weaker spirit that is bound&nbsp;
by the strength of man’s belief.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:12.000
We have, for the time being, fooled it&nbsp;
into thinking that we have overpowered it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.520
It does not understand that we do&nbsp;
so falsely: It is a god. For gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:23.520
words have Power. Ritual and belief hold greater&nbsp;
power over a god than all the laws of science.”

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:29.680
So, why are the containment procedures for&nbsp;
SCP-2845 so dramatic and complex? The answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:36.240
is simple - because the team believes the rituals&nbsp;
work. As a cosmic deity, SCP-2845 doesn't follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.600
any scientific laws as we understand them&nbsp;
on earth, but what it does understand is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:47.040
power of rituals and beliefs. The only reason&nbsp;
it hasn't escaped is that it responds to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:53.360
beliefs of the Foundation personnel, and in turn,&nbsp;
it believes that it's being held in containment.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:54.800
The consultant goes on:

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.040
“It will not think to escape, or even&nbsp;
to change its strategy. The idea will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.760
not even pass through its mind. It cannot&nbsp;
comprehend the concept. It does not think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:09.600
in the way we think. Truth be told, I would not&nbsp;
say that it thinks at all. This is an old god,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.080
it does not dabble in decisions. Decisions&nbsp;
are for creatures who may act erratically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:20.560
variably, or out of line. A god of this&nbsp;
strength simply Is. It is an absolute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:25.200
It acts as a force. In building this ritual,&nbsp;
we have shifted its being the slightest bit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:31.600
and now it is locked into a pattern of behavior:&nbsp;
It struggles against us, we struggle against it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:36.960
and we are locked together in an eternal&nbsp;
dance so long as the ritual remains intact.”

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:43.920
One last question remains, though, when it comes&nbsp;
to SCP-2845 - the rituals that are performed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:49.520
keep it in place are far from random. They seem&nbsp;
so specific that it feels impossible that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:54.000
outside consultants could've come up with them&nbsp;
out of the blue. What was their inspiration?

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:58.720
Well, in his statement to Site Director Dell&nbsp;
he mentions “listening to the songs of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:04.800
converted”. Remember how the instances of&nbsp;
SCP-2845-1 were shown to be not only alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:09.600
but communicating with each other telepathically?&nbsp;
They were able to communicate with the contractors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:14.960
as well, giving them the tools needed to create&nbsp;
the prison that would hold their god. If you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:19.680
wondering how the converted feel about having&nbsp;
been transformed into immobile green monoliths,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.200
the consultant had an answer for&nbsp;
that question, too - “They are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:27.840
suffering, but they are no longer&nbsp;
human. They are changed utterly.”

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:33.680
And so the rituals continue in order to&nbsp;
keep SCP-2845 contained. Perhaps one day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:39.200
a new technology will be found, or simpler&nbsp;
procedures will be given, but until that day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:44.080
we’re all lucky that there are others who will&nbsp;
subject themselves to horror day after day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:47.120
hour after hour, for our behalf.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:54.720
Now go check out “SCP-4205 - In The Eyes of&nbsp;
the Beholder” and “SCP-2317 - The Devourer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:59.680
of Worlds / A Door to Another World”&nbsp;
for more from the Foundation’s files!

